      "writtenOn": "2019-08-23T17:06:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What is the point of using a mix of explicit constants, and reference to another enum?\nAs far as I can tell EC_ERROR_UNKNOWN has a numerical value of 1, meaning that I2C_MASTER_IDLE and I2C_MASTER_ERROR will both have value 1, I cannot believe that to be intentional.  Even if EC_ERROR_UNKNOWN had a different value, I would be worried that a future refactoring of the EC_ constants could result in collision.",
