      "writtenOn": "2019-08-23T17:06:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The documentation of I2C_Api_MasterWrite states that the return is a \"common error code\", which I assume means EC_ series error codes.  So what is the point of \"hiding\" the particular error here, and always returning EC_ERROR_UNKNOWN.  In my opinion, you could just have\nreturn I2C_Api_Master...(...)\nin each branch, dropping both status and ret variables.",
      "revId": "008bf25cf3a197ff615176dc930d746b5c582db2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
